From 6f2ba014c6d71132fdd5246e399c561bc3cd81d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:33:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 140/140] usb: core: match root hub port DT nodes by raw port
 number
Organization: Wires

A device on a root hub port gets its device tree node from the child
of the controller node whose reg is the raw port number, the one the
host controller uses.  The port's connect type is looked up by the
logical port number instead, so the two disagree on an xHCI with both
USB 2 and USB 3 ports.

The RTL8153 on the NanoPi R2S is SuperSpeed root hub port 1, raw port
2.  With reg = <2> the device gets its node, and with it the MAC
address the boot loader stores there, but the port is not marked as
hard-wired, so usbcore.authorized_default=2 leaves it unauthorized.
With reg = <1> it is the other way around.

Signed-off-by: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/core/port.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/core/port.c b/drivers/usb/core/port.c
index 7cae19484355..92e8616e5fb2 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/core/port.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/core/port.c
@@ -740,6 +740,7 @@ int usb_hub_create_port_device(struct usb_hub *hub, int port1)
 {
 	struct usb_port *port_dev;
 	struct usb_device *hdev = hub->hdev;
+	int raw_port = port1;
 	int retval;
 
 	port_dev = kzalloc(sizeof(*port_dev), GFP_KERNEL);
@@ -752,7 +753,10 @@ int usb_hub_create_port_device(struct usb_hub *hub, int port1)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	}
 
-	port_dev->connect_type = usb_of_get_connect_type(hdev, port1);
+	if (!hdev->parent)
+		raw_port = usb_hcd_find_raw_port_number(bus_to_hcd(hdev->bus),
+							port1);
+	port_dev->connect_type = usb_of_get_connect_type(hdev, raw_port);
 	hub->ports[port1 - 1] = port_dev;
 	port_dev->portnum = port1;
 	set_bit(port1, hub->power_bits);
